## 🎯 Main Features

### 1. File upload and management

- Upload multiple CVs at once (PDF, DOCX, DOC)
- Upload JD (PDF only, 1 file at a time)
- Automatically extract and save text content from CVs to database
- Calculate SHA256 hash for each file
- Manage metadata (filename, size, content_type, upload time)

### 2. CV-JD Matching (AI Matching)

- Use OpenAI to evaluate compatibility between CVs and JD
- Return score (0-100) for each CV
- List matched and missing requirements
- Support advanced options:
  - `cvPresentation`: Evaluate CV professionalism
  - `interviewQuestions`: Suggest interview questions
  - `jobLeveling`: Assess job level
  - `certBenefit`: Analyze certificate value

## 🐛 Troubleshooting

### Error: Module not found

```bash
# Ensure dependencies are installed
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Error: Port already in use

```bash
# Change port
uvicorn main:app --port 8001
```

### Error: OPENAI_API_KEY not found

- Ensure `.env` file is created in the project root directory
- Check that `.env` file contains `OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here`
- This error only affects the `/thinking` endpoint, other endpoints will still work normally

### Database not created

- Database will be automatically created when the application starts
- Check write permissions in the project directory
- See logs at startup for detailed information

### Error extracting text from CV

- Ensure PDF/DOCX files are not encrypted or protected
- Some scanned PDF files (images) may not have extractable text
- Files will still be saved successfully, just no text content in database

### Error calling OpenAI API

- Check that API key is valid and has sufficient credit
- Check model name in `.env` (default: `gpt-4o`)
- See console logs for error details

